abstract: "A finite algebra over epistemic states, implemented as a reproducible visual notation system with enforced invariants. Four-state classification (NORMATIVE / NON-NORMATIVE / CRITICAL / METACOGNITIVE) realised as the Klein four-group V4, encoded redundantly through color, orientation, and textual label. v2.0.2 is an editorial science/citation remediation release on top of v2.0.1: it restricts the Goedel reference to a structural analogy, softens or qualifies clinical language (ego-dystonic, aporia), reframes Newton/Einstein as a limiting-case relation, aligns the metacognition / ICD 203 framing as a functional parallel rather than identity, adopts the canonical RFC 2119 / RFC 8174 / BCP 14 boilerplate, names Bertin's six retinal variables explicitly, qualifies CVD prevalence as Northern-European-descent, fixes EXPLANATION story-table overflow carryover, and removes any metaphysical overclaim from the core framing. The V4 algebra, the sigma_h assignment to METACOGNITIVE, the canonical formal sentence, the accessibility rule, and the asset set are unchanged from v2.0.1."
keywords:
